## Objective
- Autonomously hunt bug-bounty vulns on authorized scope from `data/targets.txt` (6 top-level routes on `console.byteplus.com`), proving findings with practical evidence and reporting to `result/`.
- For each top-level route: enumerate sub-routes, test client-side bugs first, then server-side.

## Important Details
- Workflow is defined by `skills/AGENT.md`; client-side methodology in `skills/client-side-skill.md`; `skills/server-side-skill.md` not yet read.
- Authorized URLs: `/waf/overview`, `/finance`, `/user`, `/beian`, `/message`, `/workorder/list/` on `https://console.byteplus.com`. No scope expansion without approval.
- Logged in with test account a: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` at `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/`. Profile: `test-user-123`, user ID `3000823185`, display name "Root test-user-123".
- Unauthenticated access redirects to `signin.byteplus.com` (out of scope); use console login path instead.
- `/waf/overview` redirects to `/iam/service/attach_role/?ServiceName=waf` (needs service-role authorization); deferred.
- `/finance` → `/finance/overview` accessible (VolcEngine finance micro-app; only same-origin sub-route anchor found: `/finance/bill/cost-analyse`).
- `/user` sub-routes from JS: `/user/basics/`, `/user/authentication/`, `/user/security/`, `/user/paymentMethod` (redirects to `/finance/payment-methods/`). React app appears escaped; only SDK postMessage listeners (Slardar/Tea) found, origin-list uses `indexOf` substring but handler is low-value.
- `/message` sub-routes: `innermsg`, `innermsg/archive`, `innermsg/detail`, `innermsg/export-task`, `iam`, `lark`, `org/config`, `org/recipient`, `org/robot`, `org/setting`, `person`, `robot`, `robot-manage`, `setting`, `verify_email`, `voice`. postMessage listener origin check is strict (`e.origin === location.protocol+'//'+location.host`). Message content is user ticket reply data.
- `/workorder/list/` sub-route: `/workorder/list/detail?id=I-...`. **Key finding path**: ticket conversation Content stored as raw HTML (`ContentFormat:"html"`) and rendered via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with NO client-side sanitization for non-markdown formats.
- CSP on `console.byteplus.com` only sets `frame-ancestors` — **no `script-src`**, so inline event handlers would execute if stored.
- Render sink: `main.7d5d0431.js` module `73868`, export `p` (= `dW`), used in `609.9d2bee7c.js` as `__html:(0,b.dW)(e)`; `dW` does innerHTML/autolink only, no sanitize. Renderer chooses markdown path only when `ContentFormat === "markdown"`.
- Markdown path uses `marked` + DOMPurify **2.5.9** with `ALLOW_UNKNOWN_PROTOCOLS:true` (module `10252` in `499.b80931e8.js`); raw-HTML passthrough only when first tag in `["span","u","br"]` (`As`/`bs`).
- **Server-side sanitization confirmed on write**: strips `on*` handlers, strips `javascript:` href → `href=""`, removes `<iframe srcdoc>` entirely, unwraps `<svg>`, adds `rel="noopener noreferrer"` (appears duplicated). Prior evidence: `<img src=x>` and `<img src="javascript:...">` stored (inert); `ContentFormat` accepts arbitrary values (prior "FOO" message) — mass-assignment via API.
- Rate limit: `{"Error":{"Code":"TooManyRequest","Message":"Request is too frequently. Please try 5 seconds later."}}` — pace ticket API calls ≥6–8s.
- Some structural mXSS payload batches return **HTTP 403 empty body** (WAF), though plain `javascript:` and `onerror` strings pass WAF.
- `ContentFormat:"html"` is sent in API body even though UI wrapper only sends `{Content,TicketID,Attachment,IsConfidential}`.
- CSRF: read `csrfToken` cookie; send header `x-csrf-token`.

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight done: tools present (opencode, curl, git, node v22.23.4, python3 3.14.4, curl 8.18.0, Chrome 156.0.8078.73), Chrome DevTools MCP connected (`http://127.0.0.1:9222`).
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md` (session metadata, run_id 40856058415, reset decision) and `result/scope.md` (in/out-of-scope, URL-list target).
- Logged in; recon on `/finance`, `/user`, `/message`, `/workorder/list/` done; JS bundles downloaded and analyzed.
- Identified prior automation tickets in account: `I-2026102917080001` ("Display name rendering probe", open/Processing, used for probes), `I-2026102903090001` (MASSTEST), `I-2026102903050001` (Cross-tenant write test), `I-2026102903040001` (CSS injection test, Closed), `I-2026102903030001` (Sanitizer mapping test, Closed), `I-2026102902580001`, `I-2026102701450001`.
- Sent stored-XSS probes to `I-2026102917080001` via `POST /api/top/ticket/ap-southeast-1/2021-01-01/CreateTicketConversation` and inspected saved Content after sanitization.
- Sanitizer mapping results so far: `onerror`→removed; `<iframe srcdoc>`→removed; `<svg><a xlink:href="javascript:...">`→`<a href="" rel="...">`; plain `<a href="javascript:...">`→`href=""`; noscript mXSS→`<p>` only; math mXSS→`<table><style>` only.

### Active
- Testing server-side HTML sanitizer bypass on ticket conversation Content, aiming for stored XSS that executes in support-agent browser (validated by watching `window.__*` flags on ticket re-render).
- Last saved probe (math mXSS) result: `MBRMATH benign:<table><style>` — only `<table><style>` survived; no handler.

### Blocked
- `/waf/overview` blocked pending IAM service-role authorization (`/iam/service/attach_role/?ServiceName=waf`) — decision on whether to authorize deliberately deferred.
- Ticket API rate-limit forces slow pacing (~6–8s between calls).
- WAF 403s on some multi-vector/mXSS payloads; need single-vector isolation.

## Next Move
1. Continue isolated sanitizer-bypass probes (one vector per request, ≥6–8s apart) on ticket `I-2026102917080001`; next candidates: `<style>` tag behavior / CSS injection, `<svg><animate attributeName="href" values="javascript:...">`, `<form><button formaction="javascript:...">`, `<object>/<embed>`, `<meta http-equiv=refresh>`, entity/whitespace-encoded `javascript:` hrefs (`java&#115;cript:`, `jAvAsCrIpT:`), `data:` hrefs.
2. After each accepted probe, reload `/workorder/list/detail?id=I-2026102917080001` and check `window.__*` flags plus DOM (e.g., `querySelector('main').querySelectorAll('img')`, iframe presence) to confirm execution vs. inert storage; if confirmed, write entry to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` per AGENT.md Section 9 and save evidence under `result/client-side/`.
3. If sanitizer holds, pivot to server-side testing: read `skills/server-side-skill.md`, then test IDOR/BAC on ticket/account APIs using both test accounts a and b, and test `redirectURI` open-redirect handling (`/user` Basics chunk module `12635`, login redirect).

